        "original_id": "416e9f68-3bc8-5e92-8290-cf34b9ab25b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Queens, Staten Island, Flushing Meadows–Corona Park\n- Products: Terrace on the Park\n- Systems: I-678, Van Wyck Expressway, Grand Central Parkway\n- Topics: population, area, foreign-born residents, location\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1899, the borough of Queens has been coterminous with Queens County.\n- In 2016, Queens had a census-estimated population of 2,333,054, making it the second-largest New York City borough by population after Brooklyn.\n- In 2016, approximately 48% of Queens residents were foreign-born.\n- In 2016, Staten Island had a census-estimated population of 476,015, making it the least populated New York City borough.\n- Staten Island is the third-largest New York City borough by area at 58 square miles.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park is located in the borough of Queens.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park lies between I-678, also called the Van Wyck Expressway, and the Grand Central Parkway.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park stretches from Flushing Bay at the southern edge of LaGuardia Airport to Union Turnpike.\n- Terrace on the Park is a banquet hall in Flushing Meadows–Corona Park.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6dab9099-fe14-59a0-99d9-66bf29c7e422",
